ty  after a long wait Diablo 4 seems to be  everything fans have been hoping for  you'd be forgiven for forgetting that at  one point Perfect Dark was one of the  most well-known and respected names in  video games given that it's been mostly  ignored since its mediocre Xbox 360  launch title but this reboot developed  by the initiative alongside Crystal  Dynamics hopes to again prove that  Perfect Dark can be relevant to the new  more modern mature industry  despite us wanting it for forever all we  know about the Elder Scrolls 6 is that  it's real and it's being worked on we  got a short teaser trailer with a title  in 2018 and that's about it so here we  are patiently waiting maybe we'll get  another Skyrim to remaster for new gen  consoles and PC in the meantime  but speaking of Bethesda and RPGs one of  the most anticipated games right now is  Starfield bethesda's sci-fi space themed  take on these Studios RPG style Todd  Howard has certainly been ambitious with  this project with thousands of planets  promised in a detailed world there's  been a trickle of Dev Vlogs if you're  interested in the development of  factions Companions and major new  locations like new Atlantis neon and  Aquila and while fans are a bit wary  after Fallout 76 and even massive  Universe games like no man's sky at  launch we'll have to see if Starfield  will measure up when it releases in 2023  that's right a new Mass Effect is coming  and hopefully it's been calibrated just  perfectly announced that the game awards  2020 the upcoming entry in the fan  favorite series still seems to be early  in development with BioWare at the helm  while the franchise has a lot to prove  after Andromeda we're ready for BioWare  to prove why Mass Effect is our favorite  Space Opera on the Citadel the teaser  had nods to the Geth Liara and Reapers  but it's unclear which of Mass Effect  3's endings if any will become Canon to  tie into this new adventure  speaking of BioWare and Redemption  stories its 